{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793743039,"nonce":"kuZWbt2pCABrD9Q7i50D0g8JmWk=","title":"Replace production surface scripts with asynchronous installed-toolchain jobs","message":"Remove the production preview path's dependency on scripts/ashui-surface.sh and sibling Rust checkout paths. The current script prefers ../ash/target/release/ash and ends by executing hybrid mode; RunPart starts it through /bin/sh and RAYDE_ASHUI_SURFACE. This is development wiring, not a distributable production contract.\n\nUse the Rust session process/job supervision and existing RunPlan/Run Configuration architecture for separate compile and launch stages, with argument arrays, configured working directory, cancellation, bounded output and responsive progress. Resolve explicit toolchain/runner configuration first, then installed executables on the session host's PATH. Package the Haxe surface shim/support and correct native libraries as versioned distribution assets rather than reaching into a RayDE/Ash source checkout. Publish real host capability/readiness and a clear missing-tool error; native/browser clients cannot infer the remote machine's paths.\n\nUser clarified that AOT can slow immediate build-and-run iteration. Do not replace hardcoded hybrid with hardcoded AOT. Honor the selected runner mode and flags. Reuse a validated existing build immediately; build changed inputs asynchronously; preserve the last good preview while the new generation compiles, then switch only on success. Hybrid remains an available fast-iteration choice; AOT can be selected explicitly or prepared ahead of time. Cache identity includes compiler/runtime, platform, shims, flags, libraries and source/macro/environment inputs. Run/Preview must not accidentally rebuild an unchanged workspace or launch stale output as current.\n\nLanding Pocket Studio specifically uses the separately prebuilt cached WASM route, so production surface rendering/AOT is not a prerequisite for its first app preview. Ordinary workspace streaming stays supported and its cold/warm build latency is measured independently.\n\nDone when a distribution-only host with no sibling repos or Bash can build and launch a configured Ashui surface, unchanged launches reuse valid artifacts, explicit hybrid/AOT settings are respected, compilation never blocks editor responsiveness, and cancellation/failure/restart retain correct process ownership. Use the existing shared command planner rather than a second hidden build system.\n\nPart of landing deployment: git-bug 56b531e22a0bf22913529f321d5b0f7d3ab02bef3d18192d73838675fff95704\nRelated Linux preview tracker: git-bug 3d6241f8d5cbe40b5ef19564282c596293c85a1d378083c13caa7fa6f8108818","files":null}]}